[TITLE]
AquaOptima dPHM-PINN Sprint 15 — small reference EPANET .inp fixture
with a pressure-reducing valve (PRV). Four-node topology:

    R1 (suction reservoir, fixed head 50 m)
      |
      +-- P1 (pipe 2000 m, 80 mm, C=130) --> J1 (elev 0, no consumer)
                                                |
                                                +-- V1 (PRV setting 20 m, 80 mm)
                                                      |
                                                      +-> J2 (elev 0; pinned by PRV)
                                                            |
                                                            +-- P2 (pipe 200 m, 80 mm)
                                                                  |
                                                                  +-> J3 (2 L/s consumer)

The dPHM importer routes the PRV row through the conservative
pressure-boundary surrogate. The downstream node J2 is pinned as a
fixed-head boundary at ``elev_J2 + setting = 20 m``; the PRV edge
itself becomes a short, permissive pipe-like resistance. This is NOT
a faithful PRV — the demand / pressure-regulation invariant is not
enforced. Mass balance on the now-fixed J2 is dropped from the
residual, so flow through V1 may differ from downstream demand. See
docs/epanet-inp-import.md for the exact assumptions and limitations.

The fixture's upstream pipe (P1) is deliberately long and narrow so
the upstream pressure budget caps the flow through V1 to a value
close to the downstream demand. This gives a physically sensible
solve even with the documented limitation.

SI flow units (LPS), Hazen-Williams head loss. Solvable by
aquaoptima.dphm.newton_solve with jacobian_mode="analytic".

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elev   Demand   Pattern
 J1   0.0    0.0      ;     ; upstream of PRV; no consumer
 J2   0.0    0.0      ;     ; downstream of PRV (pinned to 20 m by import)
 J3   0.0    2.0      ;     ; 2 L/s consumer

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID   Head   Pattern
 R1   50.0   ;          ; 50 m fixed-head suction reservoir

[PIPES]
;ID   Node1   Node2   Length   Diameter   Roughness   MinorLoss   Status
 P1   R1      J1      2000.0   80.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN
 P2   J2      J3       200.0   80.0       130.0       0.0         OPEN

[VALVES]
;ID   Node1   Node2   Diameter   Type   Setting   MinorLoss
 V1   J1      J2      80         PRV    20.0      0

[OPTIONS]
 Units                LPS
 Headloss             H-W

[END]
